cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Section Anything or its benchmark results, please cite it as below."
title: "Section Anything: PDF section and heading-hierarchy extraction"
type: software
authors:
  - alias: Omniwot
version: 0.1.1
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Omniwot/section-anything"
abstract: >-
  A Python library that finds the sections of a PDF (headings, levels, page spans and text
  ranges) using the PDF outline, typography and numbering rules, and optionally an LLM, with a
  hard cost cap. Benchmarked on READoc with READoc's own heading-tree TEDS.
keywords:
  - PDF
  - document structure
  - heading hierarchy
  - RAG
  - chunking
references:
  - type: article
    title: "READoc: A Unified Benchmark for Realistic Document Structured Extraction"
    url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/2409.05137"
    authors:
      - name: "The READoc authors"
  - type: article
    title: "HiPS: Hierarchical PDF Segmentation of Doctrinal Legal Books"
    url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.00909"
    authors:
      - family-names: Wehnert
        given-names: Sabine
      - family-names: Changaramkulath
        given-names: Harikrishnan
      - family-names: Habernal
        given-names: Ivan
